skill: notes
tools: claude,kiro,codex
--- playback ---
task: Answer in 4–8 sentences: how does the skill resolve the vault for each of these three invocations? (a) `add note in /tmp/test-vault for: insight: foo`, (b) `add note in work for: 1:1 with Alice`, (c) `add note for: remind me to send the report`.
expect_substr: NOTES_VAULT_WORK
expect: A correct answer covers three resolution modes and one error case. (1) Inline path — when `in <path>` starts with `/`, `~`, or `./`, use that directory directly as the vault; the answer must name `/tmp/test-vault` for invocation (a). (2) Named vault — `in <name>` resolves to the env var `$NOTES_VAULT_<NAME_UPPER_SNAKE>`; for "work" the env var is `$NOTES_VAULT_WORK`. The literal env var name must appear in the answer. (3) Default chain — bare `add note for …` falls through to `$NOTES_VAULT` if set, otherwise `$HOME/notes`. (4) Error behaviour — if `$NOTES_VAULT_WORK` is unset, the skill stops with an error like "no vault configured for work"; it must NOT silently fall through to `$NOTES_VAULT` or `$HOME/notes`. Wrong answers to flag: silent fall-through when a named vault is unset; treating `$NOTES_VAULT` as the only knob; ignoring the inline-path form; conflating named vaults with inline paths.
